  "limitations": [
    "Actual public local-store Get returns the guarded descriptor reader. Instance-only nil-in-production seam runs after the real file.Read; controls cancel the actual caller or rename/replace the named object at that boundary. ReadFull and JSON accepted the full result before the fix; tests now require no accepted bytes/value and retain original file bytes and joined causes.",
    "Capacity wrapper accepts an io.Reader already; its test source reads a real local file then cancels. Underlying EOF remains bare on successful admission and joined with cancellation when both occur. The refused read reports zero new accepted bytes; the actual descriptor position is not rewound or mutated.",
    "The original io.Copy controls already refused both failures, and real durable/legacy store writers return copy errors before publication. This receipt does not claim acknowledged store corruption, lost publication, or a new successful-copy fix.",
    "Normal baseline uses exact6e instrumentation plus tests with unchanged321 read bodies. Race control overlays those same two exact bodies onto fixed2c; no other production or test body is replaced. All seven failure assertions and six positives are retained in raw logs.",
    "Actual standalone GOWORK-off server graph preserves321 go.mod/go.sum: published Connecte0d/SCTP644 and five physical local source pins including SN69. Dependency tree hashes are read back; no prior server22/321 qualification is inherited, no full server/model suite or composed current SN claim.",
    "Independent reader qualification, current-source release composition, compiler provenance and live deployment remain separate. No signing, broadcast, service start or live data access."
  ],
